[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ti:29. Beauty]
[00:01.361] Passage 29. | 第29段。
[00:03.380] A young man sees a sunset, | 一个年轻人看到日落，
[00:05.745] and, unable to understand | 却无法理解
[00:07.920] or to express the emotion that it rouses in him, | 或表达它在他心中唤起的情感，
[00:10.610] concludes that it must be the gateway to a world | 从而得出结论，这一定是通往一个世界的大门，
[00:13.410] that lies beyond. | 那个世界超越了此地。
[00:14.990] It's difficult for any of us in moments of intense aesthetic experience | 在强烈的美学体验时刻，我们任何人，
[00:18.980] to resist the suggestion | 都难以抗拒这样一种暗示：
[00:20.600] that we are catching a glimpse of a light that shines down to us | 我们正在瞥见一道光芒，它从一个不同的存在领域
[00:23.950] from a different realm of existence, | 照耀着我们，
[00:26.095] different, and because the experience is intensely moving, | 那是不同的，并且由于体验是极其动人的，
[00:29.485] in some way higher. | 在某种程度上是更高的存在。
[00:31.670] And though the gleams blind and dazzle, | 尽管那些微光令人目眩神迷，
[00:34.500] yet do they convey a hint of beauty and serenity | 它们却传达出一种我们从未体验过或想象过的
[00:37.300] greater than we have known or imagined. | 更大的美丽与宁静。
[00:40.100] Greater too than we can describe, | 同时也比我们能描述的更伟大，
[00:42.258] for language, which was invented to convey the meanings of this world, | 因为语言，是为了传达这个世界的意义而发明的，
[00:45.815] cannot readily be fitted to the uses of another. | 无法轻易地适用于另一个世界的用途。
[00:48.740] That all great art has this power of suggesting a world beyond | 所有伟大的艺术都具有暗示一个超越此地世界的力量，
[00:52.620] is undeniable. | 这是无可否认的。
[00:53.715] In some moods nature shares it. | 在某些心境下，大自然也分享着这种力量。
[00:56.620] There is no sky in June so blue that it does not point forward | 六月的天空没有一片蓝得不像在指向
[01:00.100] to a bluer, | 更蓝的天空；
[01:01.010] no sunset so beautiful that it does not waken the vision | 没有一个日落美丽得不像在唤醒
[01:04.157] of a greater beauty. | 对更伟大美的憧憬。
[01:05.330] A vision which passes before it is fully glimpsed, | 这种憧憬在被充分瞥见之前便已消逝，
[01:08.520] and in passing leaves an indefinable longing and regret. | 在消逝中留下一种难以言喻的渴望和遗憾。
[01:12.350] But, if this world is not merely a bad joke, | 但是，如果这个世界不仅仅是一个糟糕的玩笑，
[01:15.750] life a vulgar shlaire, | 生命不是庸俗的玩笑，
[01:17.209] a bit the cruel radiance of the stars, | 而星星残酷的光芒，
[01:19.440] an existence an empty laugh braying across the mysteries, | 存在不是穿越神秘的空洞笑声，
[01:22.875] if these intimations of a something behind and beyond | 如果这些关于“某种存在”于其后和其外的暗示，
[01:26.055] are not evil humor born of indigestion or whimsies, | 不是消化不良或心血来潮产生的恶意幽默，
[01:29.335] sent by the devil to mock and madness, | 不是魔鬼派来嘲弄和制造疯狂的，
[01:31.740] if, in a word, beauty means something, | 换句话说，如果美有意义，
[01:34.640] yet we must not seek to interpret the meaning. | 那么我们绝不能试图去诠释它的意义。
[01:37.920] If we glimpse the unutterable, | 如果我们瞥见了不可言喻之物，
[01:40.395] it is unwise to try to utter it. | 试图说出它是不明智的。
[01:42.480] Nor should we seek to invest with significance | 我们也不应试图赋予其意义，
[01:45.145] that which we cannot grasp. | 那些我们无法掌握的东西。
[01:47.120] Beauty in terms of our human meaning | 从我们人类的意义来看，美
[01:49.595] is meaningless. | 是毫无意义的。
[01:51.405] C. A. M. Joad, | C. A. M. 乔德，
[01:53.465] Pieces of Mind. | 《思想片段》。